      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5461481::web::003::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-temperature BCC phase of Cr39Co18Fe18Ni18Al7 is stabilized by mixing entropy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cooling reduces the stabilizing free-energy contribution from mixing entropy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10056590::web::033::4_summary_and_conclusions",
        "PMC5461481::web::003::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "As the mixing-entropy contribution decreases, enthalpic differences can drive formation of a secondary phase.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10056590::web::033::4_summary_and_conclusions",
        "PMC5461481::web::003::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The secondary phase has lower free energy than BCC at lower temperatures.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5461481::web::003::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Microstructural defects or local compositional fluctuations act as nucleation sites for the transformation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slow-cooled and annealed samples will develop a measurable volume fraction of a secondary phase.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5461481::web::003::body",
        "PMC10056590::web::033::4_summary_and_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapidly quenched samples will predominantly retain the BCC phase.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12381287::web::021::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cooling rate and thermal history can significantly alter the phases and microstructure observed in multicomponent alloys.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10056590::web::033::4_summary_and_conclusions",
        "PMC12194954::web::015::4_3_spatial_temperature_field_and_melt_p"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed transformation requires processing conditions that allow the alloy to approach equilibrium, such as slow cooling and annealing.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5461481::web::003::body",
